<Begin Rant...>

Those of us reading the list as a digest form get the postings in both quoted
printable and in html format just plucked down as plain text.  In that form
they are quite UNREADABLE.  Recently we got the bug reporting system to not
forward its messages as quoted printable (thanks!!) so could us average users
PLEASE not send these horrible abominable things and stick to the universal
"plain text".

Multipart MIME goodies and the digest really don't mix.  I suppose that some
compressed patch files in base64 are a fact of life, but I can skip over them
if I don't need them.  If you desire the posting to be read by bipedal biologic
forms with brains, plain text is the way to go!!

PLEASE!!
<End Rant...>
